# Build settings: copy to ~/.config/maru/build.env (env MARU_BUILD_ENV names another path).
# Read by the web build (apps/web/vite.config.ts), the Android build and OTA export
# (apps/mobile/scripts/build-apk.sh, ota-export.mts, app.config.ts) and the desktop build.
# One KEY=VALUE per line, no shell expansion. A variable already in the environment wins.

# Android application id. It names the app on the phone and in Firebase (apps/mobile/FCM-SETUP.md),
# so a deployment keeps its value once phones have installed it. Default: dev.maru.app
# MARU_ANDROID_PACKAGE=com.example.maru

# The URL the Android app asks for OTA updates, https://<your maru server>/ota/manifest.
# Unset, the APK has OTA updates off.
# MARU_UPDATES_URL=https://maru.example.com/ota/manifest

# The certificate that holds the public key of the OTA signing key, a path relative to apps/mobile or
# absolute. Default: certs/certificate.pem. Without the file, updates are not code signed.
# MARU_UPDATES_CERT=certs/certificate.pem

# The text of Android's camera permission prompt (shown when the app first scans the pairing QR code).
# It is a native resource: a change needs a new APK. Default: Camera access is needed to scan the pairing QR code
# MARU_CAMERA_PERMISSION_TEXT=Camera access is needed to scan the pairing QR code

# Where the Bon Google Sans Code files are served (the directory that holds
# Bon-GoogleSansCode-Regular-latin.woff2 and the other files). Unset, no Bon file is downloaded and
# the chat code font falls back to the next font in its stack.
# MARU_FONT_CDN=https://cdn.example.com/fonts/v1/bon-google-sans-code

# The desktop app's application id (Windows AppUserModelID and the Mac bundle id). Default: dev.maru.desktop
# MARU_DESKTOP_APP_ID=com.example.maru

# The repository whose GitHub Releases the Android app watches for new versions, <owner>/<repo>. The app
# then offers the newest release's APK (a Download button that opens it in the browser) in place of
# the update server's notice. The public release workflow sets it to its own repository; leave it unset
# for a build that takes OTA updates from your server. Not a native input of the update fingerprint when unset.
# MARU_RELEASES_REPO=owner/repo
